@startuml playback
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Playback: Lightweight Discovery, On-Demand Continue and Queue Publication

actor "User" as User
participant "SyncService" as Service
participant "SyncRepository actor" as Repo
participant "PlaybackSyncStore\nsame repository isolation" as Store
database "Devices/<deviceID>/\nplayback.json + Queues/" as Files
participant "PlayerService" as Player

== Refresh the continue list ==
Service -> Repo : readPlayback(connectionID)
Repo -> Store : read
Store -> Repo : read(.playback, PlaybackCheckpoint)
Repo -> Files : read each device's current pointer and conflict versions (cache may hit)
Files --> Store : lightweight records
Store -> Store : highest revision per device (including tombstones)\nvalidate checkpoints; observe all revision counters
Store --> Service : checkpoints + maxCounter
Service -> Service : exclude this device / tombstones; update sessions
note over Service,Store : no full queue is read at this stage; the UI filters by the current account

== Tap on Continue ==
User -> Service : resume(selectedCheckpoint)
Service -> Service : check connection and same account\nrecord connectionID / resumeRequestID / resumingDeviceID
Service -> Repo : loadPlayback(selectedRecord)
Repo -> Store : load
Store -> Files : read only the selected queueRevision.json
alt queue missing / still downloading / invalid
  Store --> Service : downloading / invalidRecord / I/O error
  Service --> User : error for this operation; local playback kept
else queue available
  Store -> Store : check device, revision relation, account, cursor\nassemble PlaybackSession; release the previously selected queue cache
  Store --> Service : session
  Service -> Service : re-check cancellation, connection, request,\ncurrent account and that the record still exists
  Service -> Player : resume(session)
  note over Service,Player : local playback is replaced only on success; the source device is not paused
end

== Local publication check ==
Service -> Player : current session + authenticatedAccountID
alt no valid session for the same account
  opt this device has published playback before
    Service -> Repo : writePlayback(payload: nil)
    Repo -> Files : write this device's checkpoint tombstone
  end
else session content / progress changed, or not yet published
  Service -> Repo : writePlayback(record)
  Repo -> Store : write
  opt this connection has no cache of this device's published queue
    Store -> Files : read this device's old pointer and queue on demand\nto restore the reuse baseline
    note right of Store
      Old queue actually missing: the new session may publish.
      Present but not downloaded or damaged: fail explicitly, never mask it.
    end note
  end
  alt snapshot content unchanged and queue file exists
    Store -> Store : reuse queueRevision
  else snapshot content changed or file missing
    Store -> Files : first write immutable Queues/<newUUID>.json
  end
  Store -> Files : then atomically replace playback.json
  note over Store,Files : progress, current track, cursor and repeat mode live in the checkpoint;\nthe queue is not copied again
  opt first maintenance on this connection, or 24 h since the last successful one
    Store -> Files : coordinated read of current / conflict pointers;\nremove orphaned queues older than 7 days
    note right of Store
      Kept: referenced by current / conflict / previous snapshot,
      modified within 7 days, unknown file names.
      No modification date: kept until a normal maintenance cycle.
      Metadata / delete failures: logged; never fail publication or disconnect.
    end note
  end
  Repo --> Service : on success update lastPublishedPlayback / hasPublishedPlayback
end
@enduml
